{"id": "EUVD-2026-86112", "enisaUuid": "863fa497-4f25-3349-82d2-cb75b9113a6c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: chips-media: wave5: Fix Reports from Kernel Lock Validator\n\nhandle_dynamic_resolution change requires that the state_lock be acquired\nbased on the lockdep_assert_held. However, the\nhandle_dynamic_resolution_change call in initialize_sequence does not\nproperly obtain the lock before calling.\n\nSince the v4l2_ctrl_find and s_ctrl can sleep, they should not be called\nwhile a lock is already held. Store off the fbc_buf_count then properly\nupdate control once lock has been freed.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:05:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-28T05:30:50", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/629a937091ecf9c5c9f7a18f41cb0e6c778a7b2f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/072beef6a19f9c84dc5a50c5499663a5734c1096", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7d5d364f8b2dcc9b6b92456fb55632fde4a4d96f"], "aliases": ["GHSA-8mx9-7h8g-9qqg", "CVE-2026-97514"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "027272d6-b61f-3edf-a681-89b0922d83cd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9707a6254a8a6b978bde811a44fe07d86c229d1c <072beef6a19f9c84dc5a50c5499663a5734c1096"}, {"id": "18b5c912-b02e-3aec-bbab-d04b163a857e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "20088810-71e3-3c3c-bb0a-075960e418d9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "25758da6-4895-354d-aea4-40f8183d25b9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9707a6254a8a6b978bde811a44fe07d86c229d1c <7d5d364f8b2dcc9b6b92456fb55632fde4a4d96f"}, {"id": "43803fce-55e2-3721-a561-238e6688497d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "50eb088b-c599-3f30-9cae-2d7afb